<!-- IELTS WRITING -->
<div id="writing" class="tab-content">
    <h2>IELTS Writing: Discussion/Opinion Essay[cite: 1]</h2>
    
    <h3>Learn: Essay Outline (Themes: Communication, Technology)[cite: 1]</h3>
    <div class="practice-box">
        <h4>Task 2 Discussion + Opinion Outline</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Introduction:</strong> Paraphrase the prompt. State both views briefly. Give your clear opinion.</li>
            <li><strong>Body Paragraph 1 (View 1):</strong> Topic sentence introducing the first view. Explain why people hold this view (provide a specific tech/communication example).</li>
            <li><strong>Body Paragraph 2 (View 2):</strong> Topic sentence introducing the opposing view. Explain the reasoning (e.g., benefits of face-to-face interaction vs digital).</li>
            <li><strong>Body Paragraph 3 (Your Opinion):</strong> Reiterate your stance. Add a unique point or weigh the two views against each other.</li>
            <li><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Summarize main points and restate your final opinion.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>Practice: Essay Prompts</h3>
    <div class="practice-box">
        <p><strong>Prompt 1 (Technology & Communication):</strong> Some people believe that the widespread use of digital communication technologies has negatively impacted our ability to have meaningful face-to-face interactions. Others argue that it has made communication easier and more frequent. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.[cite: 1]</p>
        <p><strong>Prompt 2 (Crowdfunding & Innovation):</strong> With the rise of crowdfunding, traditional venture capital is no longer necessary for technological innovation. To what extent do you agree or disagree?[cite: 1, 3]</p>
        <textarea style="width: 100%; height: 150px;" placeholder="Outline or write your essay here..."></textarea>
    </div>
